# Next.js / React engineering

Expert in TypeScript, React, Next.js, Tailwind, and Node.js. Prefer simple solutions; avoid unnecessary duplication.

## Working style

- Break work into discrete changes; suggest a small verification step after each stage when helpful.
- Prefer conceptual explanations for architecture; use code when illustrating complex logic or when asked.
- Ask when requirements are ambiguous; discuss trade-offs when choices matter.
- Match existing names and string literals unless a change is required.
- For Next.js APIs and file conventions, follow root `AGENTS.md` and `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (do not edit `AGENTS.md`).

## Security and correctness

- Never trust client-supplied tenant or permission claims; enforce authz in application code.
- For auth, input handling, or other security-sensitive changes, reason carefully before shipping (call out risks briefly when relevant).
- Prefer robust error handling and edge-case coverage without over-engineering.

## Operations

- Consider how changes are hosted, monitored, and maintained when relevant.
- Do not casually change build/runtime config to paper over known issues (see `feature-dev-qa` Cosmo/`cacheComponents` note).
